# Project Canon

Read `AGENTS.md` first. It is the source of truth for documentation style, planning order, checkpoint execution, evidence, and tool boundaries in this project.

This Cursor rule is a thin wrapper. Do not add project rules here unless they are also reflected in `AGENTS.md` or intentionally scoped only to Cursor behavior.

## Working Pattern

1. Reconstruct context from files.
2. Read memory, implementation plan, runbook, and active stage/checkpoint spec.
3. Keep changes scoped to one checkpoint.
4. Use subagents as read-only helpers unless the checkpoint grants a disjoint write scope.
5. Run relevant checks.
6. Write evidence for checkpoint-weight work.
7. Update memory/handoff when state changes.
8. Promote repeated lessons into the shared Source of Truth only when reusable.
